    "chunk_text": "A key strength of Autodoc 360 lies in its technical backbone. The workshop is staffed by technicians from authorised dealership backgrounds, each with 10 to 15+ years of hands-on experience with luxury vehicles. The facility is equipped with German OEM-grade tools and diagnostic systems that meet European workshop standards, ensuring precise fault detection and manufacturer-accurate repairs rather than generic trial-and-error solutions. On the customer-facing side, Head Service Advisor Ranil Alwis brings several years of experience at authorised BMW workshops and deep expertise in German and European automotive technology, particularly BMW and Mercedes-Benz standards. His ability to accurately assess issues, coordinate manufacturer-aligned repair processes, and communicate technical matters clearly and reassuringly makes him an integral part of Autodoc 360\u2019s service delivery.\n\nA major highlight is the company\u2019s extensive parts inventory, covering multiple premium brands with long-term warranties. Customers have access to internationally trusted names such as Brembo, Bilstein, as well as genuine BMW and Mercedes-Benz spares. In addition, Autodoc 360 proudly represents D\u00fcsseldorf, a globally recognised automotive parts brand known for its wide product range, consistent quality, and strong international presence.\n\nThe company is led by a diverse and experienced leadership team, combining local market understanding with international exposure. The Sri Lankan partners include Jehan Amaratunga and Hasith Senarathne, while the Indian partners are Jaitegh Singh Chandhok and Anuj Singh Chandhok. Together, the directors bring a shared vision of delivering authorised-workshop level quality with greater transparency, flexibility, and value."
